<edge source="1D_CNN_3f5c2d0f" target="1D_CNN_3f5c2d0f" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 10 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 10 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 10 (for the last block of research):\n **STRATEGIC LESSON: From Capacity Hunting to Regularization Engineering**\n\n### The Consolidated Insight\nThe observed 4.2\u00d7 capacity differential between \"best\" and \"worst\" trials primarily reflects a **viability threshold** separating learnable from non-learnable regimes, not optimal architecture selection. The current \"best\" models are **brittle, overfit solutions** (20.8pp generalization gap, 23\u00d7 higher variance) that exploit specific validation folds rather than learning robust patterns. The positive correlation between dropout and accuracy likely indicates **confounding with capacity** or rescue of underfitting in oversized models, not effective regularization.\n\n---\n\n### What to Keep\n- **Minimum Capacity Threshold**: Maintain parameter counts above 600k to ensure representational adequacy; below this, task complexity cannot be captured regardless of hyperparameter tuning.\n- **Convergence Diagnostics**: Continue monitoring training dynamics (stability, learning speed) as early indicators of trainability, but treat them as diagnostic symptoms rather than causal optimization targets.\n- **Architectural Baseline**: 3\u20134 convolutional layers provide sufficient depth; deeper architectures require explicit justification via residual connections or normalization layers.\n\n---\n\n### What to Change\n1. **Success Metric**: Abandon \"mean accuracy\" as the sole objective. Adopt **Pareto optimization** maximizing accuracy while constraining generalization gap (train-test difference) to &lt;10pp and minimum fold accuracy to &gt;0.60. Current \"best\" trials fail this robustness test.\n2. **Experimental Design**: Shift from broad random search to **stratified controlled experiments**. Fix capacity at 700k\u00b1100k parameters to isolate true hyperparameter effects from the survivorship bias of \"viable vs. broken\" models.\n3. **Interaction Priority**: Test **Dropout \u00d7 Capacity** and **Depth \u00d7 BatchNorm** interactions before claiming main effects. The dropout-accuracy correlation must survive partial correlation controlling for parameter count (likely false positive).\n4. **Variance as Liability**: Treat high cross-validation variance (std &gt;0.05) as a **failure mode**, not a feature of high-performance models. Implement worst-fold accuracy thresholds to eliminate brittle configurations.\n5. **Statistical Rigor**: Apply Bonferroni correction (\u03b1=0.004); disregard current marginal p-values (dropout p=0.041, capacity p=0.023) as unconfirmed.\n\n---\n\n### The New Hypothesis\nWithin the viable capacity regime (600k\u2013900k parameters), optimal generalization is governed by **regularization-capacity coupling**, not capacity maximization. Specifically, **moderate dropout (0.4\u20130.5) paired with Batch Normalization** will outperform current high-dropout/high-capacity configurations on **minimum-fold accuracy** and **generalization gap metrics**. The previous \"best\" trials represent **over-capacitized underfitting** temporarily rescued by aggressive dropout, creating unstable convergence; true optimization requires rightsizing capacity to regularization strength while enforcing cross-validation stability.", "experiment_name": "1D_CNN", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_spectral_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "info": "SERS bacterial classification dataset - E.coli, Enterococcus, Citrobacter. Optimized for spectral peak preservation with moderate frequency resolution."}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.05450000000000001, 0.0470151319205761, 0.00037497162743048407, 1.1298242683410646, 0.27819461631774905]</data>
</edge>
