<edge source="1D_CNN_da4eef87" target="1D_CNN_da4eef87" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 20 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 20 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 20 (for the last block of research):\n**Strategic Lesson for Next Optimization Phase**\n\n**KEEP (Validated Directions):**\n1. **Capacity-Depth Coupling**: Treat high parameter counts (700k+) and depth (\u22654 layers) as necessary but insufficient conditions for top-tier performance. Maintain aggressive regularization (dropout &gt;0.5) when scaling capacity to counter the observed overfitting tendency.\n2. **Convergence Quality as Filter**: Use training stability and learning speed as early stopping criteria to filter out doomed configurations early, but recognize these metrics may reflect survivorship bias rather than causal drivers.\n\n**CHANGE (Critical Methodological Shifts):**\n1. **From Correlation to Causation**: Immediately halt \"correlation mining.\" The spectral attention finding suffers from confounding by architecture vintage and potential survivorship bias (NaN in worst trials suggests crashes, not non-use). **Mandatory**: Conduct ablation studies on the top 3 configurations\u2014remove spectral attention while holding depth and capacity constant to isolate its true marginal contribution.\n2. **Stability-First Validation**: The 3.9\u00d7 higher variance in top models (std 0.070 vs 0.018) indicates dangerous \"lottery ticket\" sensitivity. **Change selection criteria**: Replace single-run \"best\" model selection with **seed-averaged accuracy** (n\u22655 seeds) as the primary optimization metric. Discard configurations with high variance across seeds regardless of mean accuracy.\n3. **Pareto Frontier Optimization**: The inference latency penalty (10.97ms vs 8.24ms) is operationally costly. **Shift objective function** from accuracy maximization to **Pareto-optimal search** across accuracy-latency space. A 181k-parameter model at 72% accuracy dominates a 791k model at 74% if the former runs 2.7ms faster.\n4. **Correct for Multiple Comparisons**: Apply Holm-Bonferroni correction to all p-values. The dropout (p=0.0357) and depth (p=0.0194) correlations likely lose significance under correction; treat these as exploratory hypotheses requiring confirmation, not established facts.\n\n**NEW HYPOTHESIS:**\n\"Spectral attention functions as a **depth-dependent capacity multiplier** that enables efficient parameter utilization only in deep architectures (\u22654 layers) with aggressive regularization, but its benefits are **initialization-dependent and hardware-sensitive** (lottery ticket hypothesis). Therefore, robust optimization requires identifying **Pareto-optimal configurations on the accuracy-latency frontier that maintain stability (&lt;0.03 std) across random seeds**, rather than pursuing maximum accuracy through brittle, high-variance, high-capacity models.\"", "experiment_name": "1D_CNN", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_spectral_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "info": "SERS bacterial classification dataset - E.coli, Enterococcus, Citrobacter. Optimized for spectral peak preservation with moderate frequency resolution."}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.0407381, 0.04131666631579399, 0.0016495827018672767, 1.0277716441154483, 0.27354827842712404]</data>
</edge>
