  <data key="d7">{"finding": "CRITICAL ARCHITECTURAL BUG: deep_slim_residual_d_cnn.py fails catastrophically (0.3369 accuracy) when dense_units=0, despite Global Average Pooling being present. This contradicts the expected GAP behavior and indicates a structural dependency on dense layers for gradient flow or classification head compatibility. 10/30 trials (33% failure rate) affected. SOLUTION: dense_units must be \u226532 for this architecture. Winning configuration: 7 layers, 64 filters, kernel=7, dense=64, dropout=0.51, LR=0.00036, WD=0.0017 achieves 0.8923 accuracy with 0.18% overfitting gap - 70x better generalization than 1D_CNN.", "experiment_name": "1D_CNN", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_standard_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 512, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "representation_type": "1D_CNN"}}</data>
