<edge source="1D_CNN_ae58392c" target="1D_CNN_ae58392c" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 60 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 60 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 60 (for the last block of research):\n **Strategic Lesson: From Correlation to Causal Architecture Design**\n\n### Core Insight\nThe observed \"best\" trials represent an **over-parameterized local optimum** (2.68M params) engaged in a regularization arms race (dropout 0.658, weight decay 0.002) to suppress a 9.5% train-test generalization gap. The strongest predictors of success\u2014learning speed (r=0.847) and architectural features (spectral attention, residuals)\u2014are **downstream consequences** of sufficient capacity and domain-appropriate inductive biases, not independent tuning levers. The \"best vs. worst\" dichotomy reflects confounded experimental design (depth, residuals, and spectral attention likely bundled together) rather than causal mechanisms.\n\n---\n\n### What to Keep\n- **Domain Signal**: Spectral attention\u2019s perfect discrimination between best/worst trials indicates this is a frequency-domain task (audio/FFT) where standard convolutions are insufficient; this inductive bias is non-negotiable.\n- **Stability Metrics**: Convergence stability (r=0.489) and accuracy variability (r=-0.249) are valid diagnostic tools for filtering initialization noise, though they are outputs, not inputs.\n- **Depth-Capacity Relationship**: While confounded, the 6.32-layer optimum suggests the feature hierarchy requires at least 6 levels of abstraction; this is a structural constraint, not a hyperparameter.\n\n---\n\n### What to Change\n1. **Disentangle Capacity from Architecture**: The depth-accuracy correlation (r=0.596) is polluted by parameter count (r=0.351). **Fix capacity at 1.0\u20131.5M parameters** and vary depth (4 vs. 6 vs. 8 layers) by inversely adjusting width to isolate the true marginal value of depth.\n2. **Ablation over Observation**: Replace post-hoc \"best vs. worst\" analysis with **matched-pair factorial experiments**: Test spectral attention \u00d7 residual connections at fixed depths (4-layer and 6-layer) to isolate their interaction effects.\n3. **Regularization Reset**: The current 0.658 dropout indicates structural overfitting. **Cap dropout at 0.4** and reduce weight decay; if accuracy drops, the model is too large for the dataset signal.\n4. **Close the Gap**: Shift the objective from raw accuracy to **generalization efficiency**: optimize for `(heldout_accuracy - \u03b1 \u00d7 train_test_gap)` to explicitly penalize the 9.5% memorization observed in current \"best\" trials.\n5. **Add Missing Controls**: Include Batch/Layer Normalization in the search space\u2014their absence in the current analysis is a critical architectural blind spot that likely explains instability in shallow networks.\n\n---\n\n### New Hypothesis\n*The current \"best\" configuration is a high-variance, over-fit local optimum. We hypothesize that a **moderate-capacity architecture (1.0\u20131.5M parameters) with spectral attention, residual connections, and batch normalization** will achieve comparable heldout accuracy (\u00b12%) without requiring aggressive regularization (dropout &lt;0.4), thereby eliminating the 9.5% generalization gap while reducing inference latency to &lt;15ms. In this regime, learning speed becomes a diagnostic byproduct of proper architectural alignment, not a target metric.*\n\n---\n\n### Action Plan for Next Phase\n1. **Controlled Capacity Study**: Fix 1.2M parameters. Test depth 4/6/8 with width adjusted to maintain constant capacity. Measure true depth effect independent of model size.\n2. **Causal Ablation**: At the winning depth, run 2\u00d72 factorial: [Spectral Attention On/Off] \u00d7 [Residuals On/Off] to isolate component contributions.\n3. **Efficiency Frontier**: On the winning architecture, perform LR (1e-4 to 1e-3) vs. weight decay grid search with dropout fixed at 0.3 to find the Pareto frontier of accuracy vs. inference time.\n4. **Robustness Validation**: Validate top 3 configurations across 5 random seeds; discard any where convergence stability correlates with initialization rather than architecture.", "experiment_name": "1D_CNN", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_spectral_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "info": "SERS bacterial classification dataset - E.coli, Enterococcus, Citrobacter. Optimized for spectral peak preservation with moderate frequency resolution."}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.03915069743210001, 0.03614091031478048, 0.006774575881003536, 3.391524196983936, 0.35899582808303837]</data>
</edge>
