<edge source="1D_CNN_ae58392c" target="1D_CNN_ae58392c" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 65 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 65 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 65 (for the last block of research):\n**Strategic Lesson:**  \nThe analysis suggests that deeper networks with residual connections, lower learning rates (~0.0002), higher weight decay (~0.0017), and longer training (early stopping patience ~15) are associated with higher accuracy. However, these models still overfit (9.8% train\u2011test gap) and are computationally heavier. For the next phase:\n\n- **Keep:** residual connections, depth (~7 conv layers), moderate filter counts (~75), low learning rate, and higher weight decay.\n- **Change:** avoid global pooling; test whether spectral attention is actually beneficial by including trials without it; increase regularization (e.g., dropout &gt;0.6, weight decay up to 0.002) and consider data augmentation to reduce overfitting.\n- **Balance:** evaluate accuracy\u2011latency trade\u2011offs\u2014shallower or narrower models may be sufficient for deployment if accuracy loss is acceptable.\n- **Validate:** conduct a fresh hyperparameter search focusing on these promising regions, using a held\u2011out test set to confirm generalization and avoid overfitting to the validation splits. Additionally, explore interactions (e.g., depth \u00d7 residual connections) and non\u2011linear effects (e.g., learning rate sweet spot) with partial dependence plots.\n\n**New hypothesis:** Residual connections enable stable training of deeper networks, while global pooling discards task\u2011critical spatial information. With stronger regularization, the generalization gap can be reduced without sacrificing accuracy, and spectral attention may not be necessary when residual connections are present.", "experiment_name": "1D_CNN", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_spectral_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "info": "SERS bacterial classification dataset - E.coli, Enterococcus, Citrobacter. Optimized for spectral peak preservation with moderate frequency resolution."}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.039144769260889105, 0.03614091031478048, 0.0075968667647325116, 3.698602940736884, 0.35899582808303837]</data>
</edge>
