  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 80 (for the last block of research):\n**Strategic Lesson**\n\n- **Keep** the core drivers of high accuracy:  \n  - Lower learning rates (~0.0002\u20130.0005).  \n  - Deeper networks (7\u20138 conv layers) with **residual connections**.  \n  - Strong regularization: dropout (~0.6) and weight decay (~0.002).  \n  - **Avoid global pooling**; use flatten instead.  \n\n- **Change/Improve** the approach for the next phase:  \n  - **Prevent overfitting** with a strict train/validation/test split or nested cross\u2011validation.  \n  - **Perform multivariate analysis** (e.g., random forest) to isolate true hyperparameter importance and uncover interactions (e.g., depth \u00d7 residuals, dropout \u00d7 weight decay).  \n  - **Systematically vary all binary flags** (residual, global pooling, spectral attention) to quantify their impact.  \n  - **Optimize for efficiency** \u2013 test depthwise separable convolutions and reduce filters to find a Pareto\u2011optimal trade\u2011off between accuracy and model size/latency.  \n  - **Include data augmentation** and document optimizer, activation, and batch norm choices.  \n  - **Explore non\u2011linear relationships** via Bayesian optimisation to refine hyperparameter ranges.  \n\n- **New Hypothesis** to test:  \n  - Residual connections become essential when depth exceeds 5 layers.  \n  - Global pooling harms accuracy because it discards spatial information critical for this dataset.  \n  - Spectral attention provides marginal gains but may be omitted for faster inference.  \n  - A more efficient configuration (~5 conv layers, ~64 filters, tuned regularization) can achieve &gt;88% test accuracy with &lt;0.5M parameters, offering a better efficiency\u2011accuracy balance.", "experiment_name": "1D_CNN", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_spectral_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "info": "SERS bacterial classification dataset - E.coli, Enterococcus, Citrobacter. Optimized for spectral peak preservation with moderate frequency resolution."}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.039143546458729334, 0.03614091031478048, 0.008364064751879152, 4.175077153463473, 0.35899582808303837]</data>
</edge>
