  <data key="d7">{"finding": "2D_GAF Optimization Campaign Summary (22 trials): Best configuration achieved 0.9083 accuracy with kernel_size=5, filters=16, layers=6, dropout=0.85, lr=0.0005, weight_decay=0.01. Key insights: 1) Filters negatively correlate with accuracy (-0.581), 2) BatchNorm shows -1.0 correlation but may be confounded, 3) Dropout rate positively correlates (+0.679), 4) Persistent 8.7% overfitting gap, 5) Data augmentation reduces overfitting but hurts accuracy. New optimized architecture (optimized_d_gaf_cnn.py) incorporates these learnings with BatchNorm, weight decay, and proper dropout implementation.", "experiment_name": "2D_GAF", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "SERS_2D_gaf_v1", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 512, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "info": "2D Gramian Angular Field representation for SERS bacterial classification"}}</data>
